/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A state function has a fixed value once the state is fixed by properties such as P, V and T.
   - A path function depends on the route between the states.
   - X is any state function; ∮ means integration around a closed path that returns to the same state; dX is an exact differential.
   - M and N are functions of x and y; ∂M/∂y is the partial derivative of M with respect to y; ∂M/∂y is taken with x held fixed and ∂N/∂x with y held fixed.
   - Try the test on an ideal gas, with T and V as the two variables.
   - A reversible process is an ideal limit.
   - Sign rule for the whole unit: W is work done by the system and Q is heat added to it, so the first law reads ΔU = Q − W (set out in work and heat).
   - δW is small work done by the system in J; Pext is the external pressure in Pa or kPa; dV is the small volume change in m³ or L.
   - Real processes are irreversible to some degree.
   - An irreversible process cannot be reversed by an infinitesimal change.
*/
